                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Requires platforming and timing too precise for my tastes. Also the text between chapters is black on a white background. I think that adding some color could have helped, like at the beginning of the game. The visuals are at times pretty except for how the gameplay objects are animated. Things rapidly jerking one way and another makes things feel cheap, amateurish, and slapdash. The ability to slow time is useful but can also be cheesed by starting and stopping as often as you'd like. Normally the ability to slow down time would be metered to some extent. Without it, it feels like this is more of a proof-of-concept rather than a complete game.",
